  "name": "glide_back",
  "note": "(anim-rework S3 keys, real-world standard, keyed by hand; never traced) The glide backwards, weapon drawn: short steps (about 32 cm), the reaching foot checks the ground behind with the toes first and lowers the heel, the body passes back over it with the knee bent over the toes (20-28 deg), the front foot leaves heel first; feet close to the line under the hips (add 2.5), the pelvis level, the trunk at the ready stance. Phase 0 is the left toe contact behind; keys 0-0.375 are mirrored. Legs, pelvis and trunk only: the arms are keyed neutral (hanging, elbows 10) because the weapon arms stay procedural (hand IK on the gun). Angles in degrees in the body frame (x right, y up, z forward): pitch about x (+ the top forward), yaw about y (+ turns right), roll about z (+ the right side up). Pelvis offsets in cm from the standing rest. Arms: flex (+ forward, in the chest frame), abd (+ out), elbow (+ bent), inward. Legs (the Blender preview and the track only: the game's feet come from the foot planner): flex (+ the knee forward), add (+ the foot in toward the midline), knee (+ bent), ankle (+ the toes up).",
